## The short version

**Grand Baie** is a larger coastal village in the north with a population of 11 910 at the 2011 census and the Grand Baie La Croisette shopping mall. **Tamarin** is a smaller village on the west coast around a bay with surf and dolphins where the sun sets over the sea.

## Weather

Mauritius has a warm humid summer from November to April and a cooler dry winter from June to September. The trade winds bring more rain to the east of the island. The west coast is sheltered from them and is the driest and sunniest side.

## Schools and healthcare

On the Economic Development Board's list of international schools Tamarin has Paul et Virginie Primary School and Telfair International Primary School and Grand Baie has Saint Exupéry International School. Grand Baie has a private clinic in the village (Clinique de Grand Baie). From Tamarin the Artemis Cascavelle Hospital is about 9 km away.

## Property for foreign buyers

Both are popular with buyers from abroad. On the EDB's November 2022 list of Real Estate Scheme projects 15 are in Tamarin and 14 in Grand Baie. Tamarin also has the Cap Tamarin smart city. See [buying property in Tamarin](/en/living-in-the-west/buying-property-in-tamarin).

## Getting around

From Grand Baie Port Louis is about 27 km away and Ebène 42 km and the airport 71 km. From Tamarin they are about 29 and 21 and 51 km.

## Our verdict

Choose Grand Baie for a bigger place with shops and a clinic in the village. Choose Tamarin for a smaller village with surf and dolphins and west coast sunsets. Read [Living in Tamarin](/en/areas/tamarin#living).

*Figures come from the official sources listed below and were checked on 3 October 2026. Prices change so ask local agents and schools and your notary for current figures before you decide.*
